# manifest.md# Project: PhotoTriage PWA## Vision & PurposeA desktop-optimized Progressive Web App (PWA) designed to upload, view, compare, and manage photos in various formats. The application allows users to triage images efficiently (select, discard, save, delete) using a side-by-side comparison mode and a responsive grid gallery.## Core Features1. **Universal Upload:** Drag-and-drop zone for multiple image formats.2. **Gallery View:** High-performance grid layout optimized for large laptop/desktop screens.3. **Compare Mode:** Side-by-side or multi-pane view for detailed image comparison.4. **Triage Actions:** Select/Keep, Discard, Delete, and Save metadata/state.5. **Offline-First:** PWA implementation with IndexedDB for local image caching and Service Workers for app shell caching.6. **Backend:** Firebase Authentication (anonymous or email), Firebase Cloud Storage (binary files), and Firestore (metadata and triage state).## Target Devices- PC and Laptops (Landscape orientation, mouse/trackpad interactions, wide viewports).